1
00:01:58,360 --> 00:02:01,120
Students, contemplate this.

2
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:04,960
When you encounter terrible weather
like we have today,

3
00:02:05,040 --> 00:02:09,280
do you feel gloomy,

4
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:12,520
or glad that you brought an umbrella?

5
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:14,240
When you go to cross the street

6
00:02:14,320 --> 00:02:16,800
and the light suddenly turns red,

7
00:02:16,880 --> 00:02:18,480
do you feel unlucky--

8
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:20,000
Excuse me.

9
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:26,920
MENTAL HEALTH LECTURE

10
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:32,160
Do you feel unlucky?

11
00:02:32,240 --> 00:02:35,800
- Or glad that you can rest for a bit?
- My package.

12
00:02:35,880 --> 00:02:39,400
Whether someone feels happiness

13
00:02:39,480 --> 00:02:42,960
depends on their perspective of the world.

14
00:02:43,880 --> 00:02:45,320
It's not an abstract theory.

15
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:48,760
In psychology,
there is a very realistic view.

16
00:02:48,840 --> 00:02:51,120
An event itself
isn't inherently good or bad.

17
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:52,600
This is Guo Xiao's.

18
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:53,600
Some students

19
00:02:54,200 --> 00:02:55,960
don't take this lecture seriously.

20
00:02:56,040 --> 00:02:57,920
They show up when it's almost over.

21
00:02:59,040 --> 00:03:00,080
It's understandable.

22
00:03:00,160 --> 00:03:02,640
There are no credits for this lecture.

23
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:04,280
Next time,

24
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:08,360
I should apply to the college
for a mental health credit.

25
00:03:09,680 --> 00:03:10,800
No.

26
00:03:10,880 --> 00:03:12,400
No!

27
00:03:12,480 --> 00:03:13,840
All right.

28
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:16,280
Settle down. Let's get back on track.

29
00:03:16,360 --> 00:03:17,760
DELIVERY AND ERRANDS
ON-CAMPUS ONLY

30
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:19,560
Guo Xiao. Here.

31
00:03:19,640 --> 00:03:21,640
RED PACKETS RECEIVED

32
00:03:21,720 --> 00:03:22,760
Zheng Yu.

33
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:24,920
Zheng Yu!

34
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:27,680
You're walking so fast. Feeling guilty?

35
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:31,840
What is it?

36
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:35,040
Did you drop this?

37
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:36,560
It has a crack.

38
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:42,960
I did trip and fall,
but the package was in my bag.

39
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:45,360
It didn't touch the ground.

40
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:48,360
And there is cushioning in the box.

41
00:03:48,440 --> 00:03:50,880
This scratch doesn't seem
to be from the fall.

42
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:53,280
What do you mean by that?

43
00:03:53,360 --> 00:03:55,960
What I mean is
maybe it was the seller's fault.

44
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:57,960
The perfume cost 1,000 yuan.

45
00:03:58,040 --> 00:03:59,680
Are you claiming it's defective?

46
00:03:59,760 --> 00:04:01,480
I called the seller right away.

47
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:03,680
They sent me a video of it being packaged.

48
00:04:03,760 --> 00:04:05,640
The courier sent me a CCTV screenshot.

49
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:06,840
Look.

50
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:12,920
State your price for compensation.

51
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:15,000
What? You should pay the full price.

52
00:04:16,079 --> 00:04:18,360
This perfume can still be used.

53
00:04:18,440 --> 00:04:20,680
I bought it as a gift for a friend.

54
00:04:20,760 --> 00:04:23,040
I can't give them a defective product.

55
00:04:24,080 --> 00:04:26,080
Here's what we'll do.
I'll give you the perfume.

56
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:27,400
Pay the full 1,000 yuan.

57
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:31,200
I don't have 1,000 yuan right now.

58
00:04:31,280 --> 00:04:33,120
I'll give it to you as soon as I do.

59
00:04:34,920 --> 00:04:36,600
Then give me an IOU.

60
00:04:37,280 --> 00:04:38,120
Take the box.

61
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:49,840
Never mind.

62
00:04:49,920 --> 00:04:52,080
That's all. You can't renege anyway.

63
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:07,240
DR. ZHAO

64
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:12,600
Hello?

65
00:05:14,320 --> 00:05:16,120
<i>Your mom had a fever for a few days.</i>

66
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:18,560
<i>After treatment,</i>
<i>her temperature has come down.</i>

67
00:05:18,640 --> 00:05:22,040
<i>But there could be complications</i>
<i>from the prolonged coma.</i>

68
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:24,360
<i>Further medication will be needed.</i>

69
00:05:24,440 --> 00:05:26,040
<i>The fees have to be paid first.</i>

70
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:28,160
<i>The nursing fees have</i>
<i>already been discounted</i>

71
00:05:28,240 --> 00:05:29,720
<i>in accordance with hospital policy.</i>

72
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:31,800
<i>If payment continues to be delayed…</i>

73
00:06:17,320 --> 00:06:18,600
NOTICE OF HOSPITAL CHARGES

74
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:22,680
I heard the daughter
of the woman in Bed 2 is unreachable.

75
00:06:22,760 --> 00:06:24,920
She owes a huge bill. Is that true?

76
00:06:25,760 --> 00:06:28,840
Ms. Xue, where did you hear that?

77
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:33,480
The woman in Bed 2 is so unlucky.

78
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:35,160
Her son and daughter were fine,

79
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:37,400
visiting often to keep her company.

80
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:39,720
But after their uncle caused a scene here,

81
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:41,520
the son never returned.

82
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:43,400
That makes sense.

83
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:45,360
The boy was adopted by the uncle.

84
00:06:45,440 --> 00:06:47,680
Why would he care for his sick mother?

85
00:06:47,760 --> 00:06:50,440
Goodness gracious,
even her daughter has left her.

86
00:06:50,520 --> 00:06:53,000
Ms. Xue, how can you say that?

87
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:55,160
Is Xiaozheng that kind of person?

88
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:58,240
Everyone encounters difficulties
at some point.

89
00:06:58,320 --> 00:07:02,080
Saying this behind her back isn't right.

90
00:07:02,160 --> 00:07:04,200
How long has it been since she last came?

91
00:07:04,280 --> 00:07:06,040
It's not like I'm wrong.

92
00:07:06,960 --> 00:07:08,280
Xiaowu,

93
00:07:08,360 --> 00:07:09,960
how much does Xiaozheng owe?

94
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:11,920
I wouldn't know, Ms. Yang.

95
00:07:21,680 --> 00:07:24,360
I remember Xiaoliu told me
the bill was left here.

96
00:07:24,440 --> 00:07:26,000
I don't see it here.

97
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:28,160
Wait here for now.

98
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:33,760
Xiaowu, come take a look.

99
00:07:33,840 --> 00:07:35,640
My mom seems a bit feverish.

100
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:38,160
- Is she?
- It's like Ms. Xue's husband.

101
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:40,360
He had the same rash last time.

102
00:07:40,440 --> 00:07:41,360
Take a look.

103
00:07:41,440 --> 00:07:42,280
There isn't one.

104
00:07:42,360 --> 00:07:43,640
She has a rash.

105
00:07:43,720 --> 00:07:44,560
Do you see it?

106
00:07:44,640 --> 00:07:45,480
That red rash.

107
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:47,360
Could it be from the heat?

108
00:07:47,440 --> 00:07:48,320
Air out the room.

109
00:07:48,400 --> 00:07:50,360
Is it from the heat?

110
00:07:54,920 --> 00:07:55,960
Excuse me.

111
00:08:04,960 --> 00:08:06,920
<i>There is a saying I've heard.</i>

112
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:08,720
<i>You can judge a person by their shoes.</i>

113
00:08:09,680 --> 00:08:12,480
<i>Different shoes</i>
<i>take people down different paths.</i>

114
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:15,880
<i>Only the shoes on a rainy day</i>
<i>are an exception.</i>

115
00:08:16,520 --> 00:08:19,800
<i>They bring everyone</i>
<i>to a state of equal disarray.</i>

116
00:08:20,520 --> 00:08:23,760
<i>It makes me feel like</i>
<i>I am no different from them.</i>

117
00:08:54,720 --> 00:08:56,560
Excuse me.

118
00:08:58,680 --> 00:08:59,560
Thank you.

119
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:30,120
The treatment for myocarditis is
a very long process.

120
00:09:31,040 --> 00:09:32,640
Your overall recovery is good.

121
00:09:33,240 --> 00:09:35,440
But just in case,
you need regular checkups.

122
00:09:35,520 --> 00:09:37,080
Like I always say,

123
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:39,840
exercise moderately,
eat healthy, and rest well.

124
00:09:39,920 --> 00:09:42,040
If you ever feel tired, just rest.

125
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:44,320
Take care of your heart.

126
00:09:44,960 --> 00:09:45,880
Thank you, Doctor.

127
00:09:47,880 --> 00:09:49,000
Don't forget your ID.

128
00:10:05,280 --> 00:10:06,400
<i>My wallet.</i>

129
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,000
<i>It looks like this.</i>

130
00:10:31,080 --> 00:10:34,240
It has some cash and a few bank cards.

131
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:35,160
I haven't seen it.

132
00:10:35,240 --> 00:10:38,360
These are all lost-and-found items.
You can see if it's here.

133
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:42,400
LOST AND FOUND

134
00:10:45,680 --> 00:10:49,000
Why don't I make a lost-and-found notice
in our group chat?

135
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:50,240
Many people use it,

136
00:10:50,320 --> 00:10:52,440
like doctors, nurses,
and relatives of patients.

137
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:54,320
Maybe someone has information.

138
00:10:54,400 --> 00:10:55,240
Okay.

139
00:10:55,320 --> 00:10:56,680
What is your last name?

140
00:10:56,760 --> 00:10:58,280
Chen, C-H-E-N.

141
00:10:59,400 --> 00:11:00,680
Can I add something?

142
00:11:00,760 --> 00:11:02,360
If anyone finds and returns it,

143
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:04,520
I will offer a 1,000-yuan reward
as thanks.

144
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:05,880
One thousand yuan?

145
00:11:05,960 --> 00:11:07,560
Is the wallet that valuable?

146
00:11:08,280 --> 00:11:10,760
Here, take a look. Is this okay?

147
00:11:10,840 --> 00:11:13,640
- I will also need your phone number.
- Okay.

148
00:11:13,720 --> 00:11:18,120
If the lost item is very valuable,
I suggest you go to the police.

149
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:21,200
Then you will have the right
to see the security footage,

150
00:11:21,280 --> 00:11:22,720
increasing your chances.

151
00:11:23,320 --> 00:11:24,960
Okay, I see.

152
00:11:25,040 --> 00:11:26,040
Thank you.

153
00:11:43,920 --> 00:11:45,000
Is this your wallet?

154
00:11:47,280 --> 00:11:48,320
Yes.

155
00:11:59,080 --> 00:12:00,280
Where did you find it?

156
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:02,200
In the elevator.

157
00:12:13,640 --> 00:12:14,840
Thank you.

158
00:12:23,560 --> 00:12:24,840
I've returned the wallet.

159
00:12:24,920 --> 00:12:27,800
Please pay out the 1,000 yuan.

160
00:12:33,040 --> 00:12:35,000
What is the account number and name?

161
00:12:35,080 --> 00:12:36,200
I'll send it to you.

162
00:12:36,280 --> 00:12:37,440
I want cash.

163
00:12:41,520 --> 00:12:42,560
Sure.

164
00:12:56,160 --> 00:12:57,880
Hello. I found my wallet.

165
00:12:57,960 --> 00:13:00,040
Please update the post.

166
00:13:01,520 --> 00:13:04,000
Do you know that girl?

167
00:13:04,760 --> 00:13:08,160
No. She saw the post
and returned the wallet.

168
00:13:08,920 --> 00:13:10,600
It's a bit strange.

169
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:13,520
I could just be being paranoid,

170
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:17,560
but that girl was sitting
in that seating area all afternoon.

171
00:13:18,080 --> 00:13:19,200
In the beginning,

172
00:13:19,280 --> 00:13:20,480
<i>I didn't pay attention.</i>

173
00:13:20,560 --> 00:13:23,440
<i>I thought she was waiting for someone</i>
<i>or for lab results.</i>

174
00:13:23,520 --> 00:13:25,840
<i>After a few hours, I looked up,</i>

175
00:13:25,920 --> 00:13:28,280
<i>and she was still sitting there, unmoving,</i>

176
00:13:28,360 --> 00:13:29,560
just watching this desk.

177
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:31,520
Now that I think about it,

178
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:33,400
if she found the wallet,

179
00:13:33,480 --> 00:13:35,080
she could have brought it here.

180
00:13:35,160 --> 00:13:37,640
The words "Lost and Found" are
clear to see.

181
00:13:38,280 --> 00:13:39,640
Why wait all afternoon?

182
00:13:39,720 --> 00:13:42,760
So is it possible that
she was waiting for you?

183
00:13:42,840 --> 00:13:45,320
Even without the post in the group chat,

184
00:13:45,400 --> 00:13:47,520
she may have wanted to extort you.

185
00:13:47,600 --> 00:13:50,840
Do you want the police
to investigate this incident?

186
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:54,280
Forget it.

187
00:13:54,920 --> 00:13:57,040
There's no need to waste time on this.

188
00:13:57,960 --> 00:13:59,000
Thank you.

189
00:14:16,240 --> 00:14:17,120
<i>Unlocked.</i>

190
00:14:37,680 --> 00:14:38,960
Ms. Zhou,

191
00:14:39,040 --> 00:14:40,280
are you playing Werewolf?

192
00:14:40,360 --> 00:14:41,800
Night falls. Close your eyes.

193
00:14:41,880 --> 00:14:42,920
No.

194
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:45,440
The power tripped.
Your dad is in the garage fixing it.

195
00:14:46,680 --> 00:14:49,000
How was the follow-up?
Everything okay?

196
00:14:49,080 --> 00:14:50,040
No problems.

197
00:14:50,120 --> 00:14:54,240
I'll go tomorrow to fill out my paperwork.
I'll be able to take classes again soon.

198
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:55,840
That's great.

199
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:00,480
How's that?

200
00:15:01,520 --> 00:15:02,360
Not bad, right?

201
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:04,320
Wash up for dinner.

202
00:15:07,600 --> 00:15:08,640
Let's eat.

203
00:15:09,880 --> 00:15:11,880
Eat some vegetables.

204
00:15:11,960 --> 00:15:13,440
Thank you, Ms. Zhou.

205
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:20,760
Dad, you've already read every word
of my lab results.

206
00:15:20,840 --> 00:15:21,960
All right, okay.

207
00:15:23,760 --> 00:15:25,840
Are you in Yanan's classes this semester?

208
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:31,280
I'm retaking the immunology class
because of my medical leave last year.

209
00:15:32,440 --> 00:15:36,360
I'm glad your mom's childhood friend
can watch over you.

210
00:15:36,440 --> 00:15:37,600
Watch over me?

211
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:39,640
Then remember to pay him.

212
00:15:41,240 --> 00:15:43,360
Right, speaking of which, that reminds me.

213
00:15:44,880 --> 00:15:47,360
Give this to him for me.

214
00:15:47,440 --> 00:15:50,280
Write some auspicious words on it as well.

215
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:52,920
I was kidding.

216
00:15:54,200 --> 00:15:55,240
No.

217
00:15:55,920 --> 00:15:58,200
He just moved. It's a housewarming gift.

218
00:16:04,280 --> 00:16:05,560
HAPPY HOUSEWARMING

219
00:16:05,640 --> 00:16:07,520
Ms. Zhou asked me to give this to you.

220
00:16:15,320 --> 00:16:16,520
Did you write this?

221
00:16:16,600 --> 00:16:17,440
Obviously.

222
00:16:18,040 --> 00:16:19,240
The ink just dried.

223
00:16:20,280 --> 00:16:22,480
Pretty nice Zhao-style calligraphy.

224
00:16:22,560 --> 00:16:23,760
I'll take it.

225
00:16:23,840 --> 00:16:25,080
However,

226
00:16:25,880 --> 00:16:27,320
she and I are old friends.

227
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:29,040
She didn't have to give money.

228
00:16:29,600 --> 00:16:31,920
Besides, she isn't coming
to the housewarming.

229
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:33,440
A gift isn't necessary.

230
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:35,000
Accept it.

231
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:38,080
YOU RECEIVED 1,000 YUAN

232
00:16:38,880 --> 00:16:41,640
This gifting back and forth
only troubles me.

233
00:16:42,240 --> 00:16:43,440
All right.

234
00:16:43,520 --> 00:16:44,720
It's exam time. Go.

235
00:16:45,920 --> 00:16:49,080
You're lucky to make it in time
for my in-class exam.

236
00:16:49,160 --> 00:16:51,560
This is counted towards the regular grade.

237
00:16:52,800 --> 00:16:54,480
If I do well on this exam,

238
00:16:54,560 --> 00:16:56,760
give me the key to the old lab.

239
00:16:56,840 --> 00:16:58,920
I live off-campus.
I need a place to study.

240
00:16:59,640 --> 00:17:00,840
I knew it.

241
00:17:00,920 --> 00:17:02,440
A housewarming gift?

242
00:17:02,520 --> 00:17:04,720
There was an ulterior motive.

243
00:17:12,119 --> 00:17:13,560
Before we begin today's exam,

244
00:17:13,640 --> 00:17:15,680
I want to introduce someone new.

245
00:17:16,319 --> 00:17:17,160
Chen Yanzhou.

246
00:17:17,240 --> 00:17:19,119
He's a year older than you.

247
00:17:19,200 --> 00:17:22,040
He took a year off for medical reasons.

248
00:17:22,119 --> 00:17:24,319
Starting today, he is joining Class 1.

249
00:17:24,400 --> 00:17:27,640
I'm sure you will have
many classes together,

250
00:17:27,720 --> 00:17:30,200
so please get along well.

251
00:17:32,800 --> 00:17:34,000
You can sit over there.

252
00:17:35,240 --> 00:17:36,520
Zheng Yu.

253
00:17:36,600 --> 00:17:37,480
Here.

254
00:17:52,360 --> 00:17:53,520
Zheng Yu.

255
00:17:54,120 --> 00:17:56,200
You don't have a lab partner
this semester, right?

256
00:17:56,280 --> 00:17:58,200
You and Chen Yanzhou will be partners.

257
00:18:02,360 --> 00:18:03,640
Okay, put everything away.

258
00:18:03,720 --> 00:18:04,920
Get ready for the exam.

259
00:18:23,680 --> 00:18:24,760
Hey.

260
00:18:26,400 --> 00:18:28,760
Find a reason to give Mr. Li.

261
00:18:28,840 --> 00:18:30,960
Any reason. Just don't be my partner.

262
00:18:33,800 --> 00:18:36,280
- What do you mean?
- Weren't you away for a year?

263
00:18:36,880 --> 00:18:39,400
I don't have time to help you catch up.

264
00:18:41,960 --> 00:18:44,040
In that case, why did you agree earlier?

265
00:18:44,840 --> 00:18:47,200
You get to be the good guy,
and I'm the bad guy.

266
00:18:48,160 --> 00:18:51,800
I didn't want to reject you
and embarrass you in front of everyone.

267
00:18:55,320 --> 00:18:56,280
Should I thank you?

268
00:18:56,880 --> 00:18:58,040
No need.

269
00:18:58,120 --> 00:19:00,480
You can tell Mr. Li that I'm the problem.

270
00:19:01,080 --> 00:19:02,360
I have better things to do.

271
00:19:19,480 --> 00:19:21,040
Cutting it close again.

272
00:19:22,920 --> 00:19:24,560
Do kids nowadays refuse to give

273
00:19:24,640 --> 00:19:27,080
even an extra minute
of their lives to work?

274
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:32,440
Who is the boss here?

275
00:19:33,960 --> 00:19:35,960
Hurry up and ring them up.

276
00:19:40,600 --> 00:19:42,400
When are you going to pay me
for the perfume?

277
00:19:42,480 --> 00:19:43,400
It's been days.

278
00:19:45,080 --> 00:19:47,080
When I get the Vitality Award.

279
00:19:47,840 --> 00:19:49,360
The Vitality Award?

280
00:19:50,040 --> 00:19:53,040
Only the top student
in each major can get it.

281
00:19:53,800 --> 00:19:56,200
Can you be 100% certain you can get it?

282
00:19:56,280 --> 00:19:57,880
I got it for the past two years.

283
00:19:57,960 --> 00:20:00,400
It shouldn't be a problem this year.

284
00:20:01,800 --> 00:20:03,360
Cash or scan to pay?

285
00:20:08,600 --> 00:20:09,440
Fine.

286
00:20:09,520 --> 00:20:10,760
It's just a few months.

287
00:20:11,360 --> 00:20:12,680
Even if you don't get it,

288
00:20:13,280 --> 00:20:15,520
the general scholarship is
more than enough.

289
00:20:16,320 --> 00:20:17,160
I have a request.

290
00:20:17,760 --> 00:20:20,040
I want your help
on my elective assignments

291
00:20:20,120 --> 00:20:20,960
as interest.

292
00:20:22,840 --> 00:20:23,680
Fine.

293
00:21:07,640 --> 00:21:08,520
Paying in cash.

294
00:21:11,560 --> 00:21:12,840
A total of 66 yuan.

295
00:21:24,040 --> 00:21:25,320
So much for being

296
00:21:26,280 --> 00:21:27,880
a Vitality Award recipient.

297
00:21:42,440 --> 00:21:44,000
Your time doesn't seem

298
00:21:44,640 --> 00:21:46,120
as valuable as you say.

299
00:22:49,120 --> 00:22:50,520
<i>One just-expired rice ball.</i>

300
00:22:51,040 --> 00:22:52,560
<i>Two just-expired boxed meals.</i>

301
00:22:53,960 --> 00:22:56,200
LU SIQUAN

302
00:23:13,520 --> 00:23:15,800
<i>"Just expired"?</i>
<i>Those expired four hours ago!</i>

303
00:23:16,400 --> 00:23:17,520
<i>Toss them earlier.</i>

304
00:23:17,600 --> 00:23:19,880
<i>Don't wait until it's night</i>
<i>to slowly check them.</i>

305
00:24:00,480 --> 00:24:01,320
Thank you.

306
00:24:02,080 --> 00:24:03,440
Zheng Yu, you're back.

307
00:24:03,520 --> 00:24:05,880
These are the new roommates
I told you about.

308
00:24:05,960 --> 00:24:08,760
They moved from the fifth floor
and are in Class 2.

309
00:24:09,680 --> 00:24:11,160
This is Liu Linlin.

310
00:24:11,240 --> 00:24:12,080
Hello.

311
00:24:12,160 --> 00:24:13,840
We're in many classes together.

312
00:24:15,400 --> 00:24:16,240
This is Xu--

313
00:24:16,320 --> 00:24:17,520
I'm Xu Fangli.

314
00:24:17,600 --> 00:24:19,920
Is your WeChat profile picture blank?

315
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:21,640
Do you know each other?

316
00:24:22,240 --> 00:24:23,800
She's helped me with errands.

317
00:24:24,640 --> 00:24:27,720
You always collected the luggage
I had sent over each semester.

318
00:24:28,400 --> 00:24:30,360
You did it even without an elevator.

319
00:24:30,440 --> 00:24:32,240
It was a paid service,
not a favor to thank me for.

320
00:24:32,880 --> 00:24:33,800
Why not?

321
00:24:33,880 --> 00:24:37,080
Without you,
I don't know how I would've managed.

322
00:24:37,680 --> 00:24:39,640
Couldn't you just bring it with you?

323
00:24:39,720 --> 00:24:41,280
Why did it have to be sent?

324
00:24:41,360 --> 00:24:43,360
Traveling with luggage is such a hassle.

325
00:24:43,960 --> 00:24:45,200
Best to travel light.

326
00:24:45,800 --> 00:24:47,480
Even a big handbag is too much.

327
00:24:51,720 --> 00:24:53,120
Is our stuff in your way?

328
00:24:54,120 --> 00:24:56,680
We heard two of your roommates
moved off-campus,

329
00:24:56,760 --> 00:24:58,400
so we applied to move down here.

330
00:24:58,480 --> 00:24:59,880
I can't believe you're here.

331
00:24:59,960 --> 00:25:02,000
It's good to see a familiar face.

332
00:25:03,720 --> 00:25:04,840
Sorry.

333
00:25:04,920 --> 00:25:07,800
Your desk was empty,
so I borrowed it for a bit.

334
00:25:07,880 --> 00:25:08,720
Thank you.

335
00:25:10,680 --> 00:25:11,680
Thank you.

336
00:25:11,760 --> 00:25:13,560
One, two, three, go.

337
00:25:19,280 --> 00:25:20,320
Had a light dinner?

338
00:25:21,120 --> 00:25:22,800
No, I didn't even eat.

339
00:25:23,400 --> 00:25:24,840
I thought of it as dieting.

340
00:25:24,920 --> 00:25:27,960
I didn't expect this bit of work
to use up so much energy.

341
00:25:28,760 --> 00:25:29,600
This…

342
00:25:30,920 --> 00:25:32,080
At this hour,

343
00:25:32,160 --> 00:25:33,400
the doors will be closed.

344
00:25:35,440 --> 00:25:38,000
It's fine. Missing one meal won't kill me.

345
00:25:51,480 --> 00:25:52,640
Zheng Yu,

346
00:25:52,720 --> 00:25:54,800
can you sell your other meal to me?

347
00:25:54,880 --> 00:25:57,240
I can treat you
to anything you want tomorrow.

348
00:26:07,280 --> 00:26:08,160
Sorry.

349
00:26:08,720 --> 00:26:10,560
This is my breakfast for tomorrow.

350
00:26:14,720 --> 00:26:17,080
It's okay. I guess it will help me
lose some weight.

351
00:26:29,360 --> 00:26:31,120
Today's practical lab has one goal.

352
00:26:31,200 --> 00:26:33,480
That is to make target bands visible.

353
00:26:33,560 --> 00:26:34,520
Remember.

354
00:26:34,600 --> 00:26:37,080
Adhering to safety protocols
and careful execution

355
00:26:37,160 --> 00:26:40,040
are the sole prerequisites
for achieving visible bands.

356
00:26:46,640 --> 00:26:49,240
Let me also mention the competition.

357
00:26:49,320 --> 00:26:50,160
This semester,

358
00:26:50,240 --> 00:26:53,520
we'll be having the Excellence Cup
College Student Life Sciences Competition.

359
00:26:53,600 --> 00:26:55,760
Why am I making you
do experiments in teams?

360
00:26:55,840 --> 00:26:57,400
It's so you learn to get along.

361
00:26:58,160 --> 00:26:59,040
Now,

362
00:26:59,120 --> 00:27:01,760
there are two months
until the registration deadline.

363
00:27:01,840 --> 00:27:02,680
So

364
00:27:03,760 --> 00:27:04,800
team up early

365
00:27:05,480 --> 00:27:06,880
and prepare in advance.

366
00:27:10,400 --> 00:27:11,520
Team up.

367
00:27:21,920 --> 00:27:24,760
Didn't I tell you two to partner up?

368
00:27:24,840 --> 00:27:25,680
What's going on?

369
00:27:30,400 --> 00:27:31,760
I think going solo is fine.

370
00:27:31,840 --> 00:27:34,160
The concept of teamwork is a hoax.

371
00:27:34,240 --> 00:27:37,280
A team of two people at different levels

372
00:27:37,360 --> 00:27:39,160
receives the same score.

373
00:27:39,680 --> 00:27:41,640
Only the one with lower grades

374
00:27:42,160 --> 00:27:43,800
would find it fair.

375
00:27:45,120 --> 00:27:46,920
You two haven't teamed up before.

376
00:27:47,000 --> 00:27:49,240
I have partnered with others before.

377
00:27:49,880 --> 00:27:51,440
But every time,

378
00:27:52,040 --> 00:27:53,080
my partner

379
00:27:53,760 --> 00:27:54,800
was a burden to me.

380
00:27:58,640 --> 00:28:00,040
Actually, Chen Yanzhou--

381
00:28:00,120 --> 00:28:01,120
I agree.

382
00:28:01,200 --> 00:28:02,120
Sir,

383
00:28:02,720 --> 00:28:05,120
I took a break from my studies for a year.

384
00:28:05,200 --> 00:28:07,200
I don't want to hold others back.

385
00:28:10,200 --> 00:28:11,600
Since we are in agreement,

386
00:28:11,680 --> 00:28:12,640
this talk is over.

387
00:28:13,320 --> 00:28:16,200
Sir, I'm busy. I have to go.

388
00:28:23,800 --> 00:28:24,840
Hold others back?

389
00:28:25,760 --> 00:28:29,360
Before you took time off, you were
already studying third-year courses.

390
00:28:29,440 --> 00:28:31,440
You kept up your studies while away.

391
00:28:32,360 --> 00:28:33,760
You didn't tell Zheng Yu.

392
00:28:34,400 --> 00:28:35,920
What would I tell her?

393
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:39,240
That I might not be
the one on a lower level?

394
00:28:40,920 --> 00:28:44,080
Not only are you healthier,
but your words have become harsher.

395
00:28:44,160 --> 00:28:46,160
So you agree it's harsh.

396
00:28:46,240 --> 00:28:47,160
I just copied her.

397
00:28:50,200 --> 00:28:52,800
Give the Excellence Cup some thought.

398
00:28:54,040 --> 00:28:55,920
Zheng Yu is a good choice.

399
00:28:56,000 --> 00:28:58,160
She's a two-year Vitality Award recipient.

400
00:28:58,240 --> 00:29:00,880
It's just that you don't know her well.

401
00:29:02,040 --> 00:29:03,440
I do know her.

402
00:29:03,520 --> 00:29:04,720
You do?

403
00:29:06,840 --> 00:29:10,040
I recently learned
that some people use their scholarship

404
00:29:10,120 --> 00:29:11,360
like a credit card

405
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:13,200
to buy now, pay later.

406
00:29:26,560 --> 00:29:27,440
Hello.

407
00:29:27,520 --> 00:29:31,360
- Do you have this brand of beef?
- Let me see.

408
00:29:32,520 --> 00:29:33,800
It should be sold out.

409
00:29:33,880 --> 00:29:36,040
I'll check out the back.
There might be some.

410
00:29:36,640 --> 00:29:37,480
Okay.

411
00:29:38,920 --> 00:29:41,440
Ms. Zhou, I'm at the supermarket.

412
00:29:41,520 --> 00:29:43,200
Is there anything you need?

413
00:29:43,280 --> 00:29:46,040
<i>I thought you were</i>
<i>going to the lab tonight.</i>

414
00:29:46,120 --> 00:29:47,360
Dad is working late.

415
00:29:47,440 --> 00:29:51,400
Having dinner with you is more important
than doing experiments.

416
00:30:12,440 --> 00:30:13,600
Hello, miss.

417
00:30:14,440 --> 00:30:16,200
We're out of the imported beef.

418
00:30:16,280 --> 00:30:18,800
This is similar in cost
and quality. Is that okay?

419
00:30:18,880 --> 00:30:20,200
Okay, I'll take it.

420
00:30:30,320 --> 00:30:31,160
I'm in a hurry.

421
00:30:32,080 --> 00:30:33,240
What's your point?

422
00:30:37,600 --> 00:30:39,360
<i>Item successful.</i>

423
00:30:39,920 --> 00:30:41,640
That's 1,321 yuan.

424
00:30:42,440 --> 00:30:44,200
Here's your receipt. Take it.

425
00:30:49,600 --> 00:30:51,480
She doesn't look short on cash.

426
00:31:09,960 --> 00:31:12,800
Don't get my imported rug dirty,

427
00:31:12,880 --> 00:31:14,720
or you'll have to pay in US dollars.

428
00:31:15,480 --> 00:31:16,560
Shoes.

429
00:31:32,920 --> 00:31:35,120
Why are you putting it there?
Put it on the counter.

430
00:31:37,880 --> 00:31:40,080
I've been calling you for ages,
but you didn't answer.

431
00:31:40,160 --> 00:31:43,680
My son's tutoring lesson
was supposed to start 15 minutes ago.

432
00:31:43,760 --> 00:31:46,400
Due to your poor time management,

433
00:31:46,480 --> 00:31:49,080
my son's bedtime will have to be
pushed back 15 minutes.

434
00:31:50,800 --> 00:31:52,160
The total is 1,321 yuan.

435
00:31:52,240 --> 00:31:54,480
You sent 1,300 yuan, 21 yuan short.

436
00:31:58,720 --> 00:32:01,120
Who told you to buy this brand of beef?

437
00:32:01,200 --> 00:32:04,520
You're a college student,
and you can't even do this correctly.

438
00:32:04,600 --> 00:32:07,080
You can exchange it
at the store with the receipt.

439
00:32:08,360 --> 00:32:09,320
What a hassle.

440
00:32:10,120 --> 00:32:12,400
You're right that it is a hassle.

441
00:32:12,480 --> 00:32:14,040
If you need errands done,

442
00:32:14,120 --> 00:32:15,960
please pay the errand fee in advance.

443
00:32:16,040 --> 00:32:19,760
It's now 20 minutes
past the original tutoring start time.

444
00:32:19,840 --> 00:32:23,280
I will go start the lesson now
so your son doesn't stay up all night.

445
00:32:24,600 --> 00:32:25,440
You…

446
00:32:31,800 --> 00:32:34,280
Ms. Zheng, do you hate my mom?

447
00:32:35,560 --> 00:32:36,520
I don't love her.

448
00:32:37,240 --> 00:32:40,480
Then why don't you
just tutor somewhere else?

449
00:32:41,240 --> 00:32:42,920
Your house is close to the campus.

450
00:32:45,000 --> 00:32:48,560
Aren't you afraid she will fire you
if you treat her like that?

451
00:32:49,720 --> 00:32:50,560
What have I done?

452
00:32:52,080 --> 00:32:54,440
Talked back to her. Defied her.

453
00:32:54,520 --> 00:32:56,280
For the amount she pays me,

454
00:32:56,360 --> 00:32:57,600
she probably can't find

455
00:32:57,680 --> 00:33:00,120
another college student tutor
offering better value.

456
00:33:00,200 --> 00:33:03,000
I have the grades and ranking she likes.

457
00:33:03,080 --> 00:33:05,400
EXAM SCORE: 95,
NAME: ZHENG YU, RANK: SECOND

458
00:33:07,280 --> 00:33:09,120
Couldn't Yanan give me another point?

459
00:33:09,200 --> 00:33:10,480
Make it an even number.

460
00:33:11,000 --> 00:33:13,040
You think you're haggling for groceries?

461
00:33:13,120 --> 00:33:16,040
Say, I crammed day and night,

462
00:33:16,120 --> 00:33:17,560
and this is all I got.

463
00:33:17,640 --> 00:33:21,160
This Chen Yanzhou took nearly a year off.

464
00:33:21,240 --> 00:33:22,920
His grades aren't affected at all.

465
00:33:23,000 --> 00:33:26,480
I heard from an upperclassman that
their student year has a saying.

466
00:33:26,560 --> 00:33:29,040
There's no first place
that Chen Yanzhou can't get.

467
00:33:29,120 --> 00:33:30,840
Unless he doesn't participate.

468
00:33:30,920 --> 00:33:32,200
- Yeah, right.
- It's true.

469
00:33:32,880 --> 00:33:34,760
He got into Cheng Xiulin's lab
in his freshman year.

470
00:33:34,840 --> 00:33:38,880
It seems that he later had to withdraw
due to medical reasons.

471
00:33:39,480 --> 00:33:40,640
He's a serious student.

472
00:33:41,560 --> 00:33:43,320
He always got the Vitality Award.

473
00:33:44,200 --> 00:33:45,960
NAME: ZHENG YU, RANK: SECOND

474
00:33:52,840 --> 00:33:55,280
<i>Last week,</i>
<i>you paid 2,000 yuan just in time.</i>

475
00:33:55,360 --> 00:33:57,040
<i>But this won't last long.</i>

476
00:33:57,120 --> 00:33:59,200
<i>Can you come up with another solution?</i>

477
00:34:06,000 --> 00:34:06,960
Geez.

478
00:34:07,560 --> 00:34:09,320
Where are you going? Class is starting.

479
00:34:11,000 --> 00:34:12,120
In a bad mood?

480
00:34:18,920 --> 00:34:20,960
"Where are you going? Class is starting."

481
00:34:22,840 --> 00:34:24,159
It's been three years.

482
00:34:24,239 --> 00:34:25,560
You still like Zheng Yu?

483
00:34:26,239 --> 00:34:27,880
He's a hopeless romantic.

484
00:34:42,920 --> 00:34:44,719
<i>Before the immunology exam,</i>

485
00:34:44,800 --> 00:34:46,960
<i>I saw that repeat student</i>
<i>give a red packet</i>

486
00:34:47,040 --> 00:34:48,400
<i>to Li Yanan.</i>

487
00:35:08,240 --> 00:35:09,520
After class,

488
00:35:10,840 --> 00:35:11,840
let's talk.

489
00:35:24,640 --> 00:35:26,880
You don't want to sit
at the same table as me,

490
00:35:26,960 --> 00:35:28,440
so just get to the point.

491
00:35:31,160 --> 00:35:32,840
Before the immunology exam,

492
00:35:32,920 --> 00:35:34,800
you gave Mr. Li a red packet.

493
00:35:42,400 --> 00:35:43,240
Who said that?

494
00:35:43,320 --> 00:35:44,760
It doesn't matter.

495
00:35:47,720 --> 00:35:48,960
Most people who hear that

496
00:35:49,640 --> 00:35:53,120
would gossip behind my back
or directly report me.

497
00:35:53,920 --> 00:35:56,320
I've never met someone like you.

498
00:35:56,840 --> 00:35:58,000
I thought about it.

499
00:35:58,080 --> 00:36:01,240
Mr. Li doesn't seem like
the type to accept bribes.

500
00:36:01,840 --> 00:36:04,000
I don't want
to arbitrarily gossip or report

501
00:36:04,080 --> 00:36:06,360
and cause harm to a responsible teacher.

502
00:36:06,960 --> 00:36:08,960
But nothing is absolute.

503
00:36:10,000 --> 00:36:11,440
So I wanted to ask you.

504
00:36:12,160 --> 00:36:13,480
I want to confirm,

505
00:36:13,560 --> 00:36:15,000
at least in this matter,

506
00:36:15,920 --> 00:36:16,920
that all was fair.

507
00:36:20,240 --> 00:36:22,000
What if it was unfair

508
00:36:22,080 --> 00:36:23,520
and I did give it to him?

509
00:36:25,240 --> 00:36:26,400
What will you do?

510
00:36:30,000 --> 00:36:32,120
Well, I don't want you to be unaware,

511
00:36:32,200 --> 00:36:34,680
walking around the campus without a care.

512
00:36:35,320 --> 00:36:38,720
I have to at least let you know
that I know what you did.

513
00:36:41,000 --> 00:36:43,120
"I know what you did."

514
00:36:44,520 --> 00:36:46,080
That should be my sentence.

515
00:36:47,400 --> 00:36:49,960
Li Yanan never received my money.

516
00:36:50,040 --> 00:36:51,200
Did you forget?

517
00:36:52,320 --> 00:36:53,760
The one who got money from me

518
00:36:53,840 --> 00:36:54,960
was you.

519
00:36:55,800 --> 00:36:57,480
I never got the chance to ask you.

520
00:36:58,080 --> 00:36:59,640
How did you find my wallet?

521
00:36:59,720 --> 00:37:01,720
If there hadn't been
a lost-and-found notice

522
00:37:01,800 --> 00:37:04,040
when you found my wallet,

523
00:37:04,120 --> 00:37:07,200
what price would you have demanded?

524
00:37:20,680 --> 00:37:21,800
JOB RATES
SEND?

525
00:37:24,760 --> 00:37:27,280
COLLEGE OF FOREIGN LANGUAGES
QIAN YIWEN, 500 YUAN

526
00:37:27,360 --> 00:37:28,440
ACCEPT?

527
00:37:28,520 --> 00:37:29,840
LOADING

528
00:37:30,360 --> 00:37:31,200
QIAN YIWEN

529
00:37:31,280 --> 00:37:33,440
<i>Have you chosen football</i>
<i>for your PE class?</i>

530
00:37:34,040 --> 00:37:36,280
<i>Does the football instructor know you?</i>

531
00:37:36,880 --> 00:37:38,520
<i>No, he doesn't.</i>

532
00:37:41,400 --> 00:37:42,760
Welcome.

533
00:37:46,480 --> 00:37:47,520
<i>Great!</i>

534
00:37:48,640 --> 00:37:49,800
Shi Yinjie.

535
00:37:49,880 --> 00:37:50,720
Here.

536
00:37:51,440 --> 00:37:53,280
- Shen Lei.
- Here.

537
00:37:53,360 --> 00:37:54,440
Qian Yiwen.

538
00:37:55,920 --> 00:37:57,120
Qian Yiwen!

539
00:37:59,360 --> 00:38:00,520
Zhong Qiu.

540
00:38:02,360 --> 00:38:03,480
All right.

541
00:38:03,560 --> 00:38:04,880
Next, for this class--

542
00:38:04,960 --> 00:38:05,800
Sir.

543
00:38:06,480 --> 00:38:09,280
My name wasn't called.
I applied for the class last week.

544
00:38:09,960 --> 00:38:11,280
What is your name?

545
00:38:11,360 --> 00:38:12,360
Chen Yanzhou.

546
00:38:12,960 --> 00:38:13,960
I didn't receive it.

547
00:38:14,560 --> 00:38:16,280
You can follow along.

548
00:38:16,360 --> 00:38:18,440
Get this sorted after class.

549
00:38:20,240 --> 00:38:21,600
- Next, let's--
- Sir!

550
00:38:25,720 --> 00:38:27,080
I'm Qian Yiwen.

551
00:38:29,000 --> 00:38:30,160
Fall in quickly.

552
00:38:33,720 --> 00:38:34,760
I remember you were

553
00:38:35,360 --> 00:38:36,960
nearly late last time too.

554
00:38:38,480 --> 00:38:39,320
Yes.

555
00:38:40,040 --> 00:38:41,200
Don't do it again.

556
00:38:41,280 --> 00:38:42,640
If you do it again,

557
00:38:42,720 --> 00:38:44,000
you will be marked tardy.

558
00:38:45,600 --> 00:38:47,480
Don't assume I don't know who you are.

559
00:38:48,080 --> 00:38:49,880
I'm keeping tabs on each of you.

560
00:38:52,600 --> 00:38:53,720
QIAN YIWEN

561
00:38:53,800 --> 00:38:54,960
Fall in.

562
00:38:55,720 --> 00:38:57,760
Okay, go to the field.

563
00:38:58,360 --> 00:39:01,800
For this class, practice with a partner
what you learned last time,

564
00:39:01,880 --> 00:39:04,200
kicking the ball
with the inside of your foot.

565
00:39:04,280 --> 00:39:05,640
Practice for 20 minutes.

566
00:39:05,720 --> 00:39:07,760
After that, we'll learn something new.

567
00:39:07,840 --> 00:39:09,240
Okay, get to it.

568
00:39:16,000 --> 00:39:17,960
<i>Who is your football partner?</i>

569
00:39:18,040 --> 00:39:19,480
<i>I'm solo right now.</i>

570
00:39:19,560 --> 00:39:22,320
<i>If this keeps up, the instructor</i>
<i>will eventually notice.</i>

571
00:39:22,400 --> 00:39:24,240
<i>We'll be in trouble.</i>

572
00:39:24,840 --> 00:39:25,920
Got it? Like that.

573
00:39:26,000 --> 00:39:27,320
The top of the foot.

574
00:39:28,760 --> 00:39:31,960
<i>I forgot to tell you.</i>
<i>My partner also cut class today.</i>

575
00:39:32,560 --> 00:39:34,880
<i>Why don't you just pick someone there?</i>

576
00:39:35,480 --> 00:39:36,960
<i>Extra charge.</i>

577
00:39:38,920 --> 00:39:40,120
Again.

578
00:39:41,160 --> 00:39:42,280
Get it this time.

579
00:39:47,880 --> 00:39:48,960
Hey there!

580
00:39:55,360 --> 00:39:56,840
Hey, are you okay?

581
00:39:56,920 --> 00:39:57,760
It's an accident.

582
00:40:03,320 --> 00:40:06,240
I wanted to ask you
if you wanted to practice together.

583
00:40:07,440 --> 00:40:08,480
No.

584
00:40:16,320 --> 00:40:17,400
How are you? Okay?

585
00:40:19,680 --> 00:40:22,200
Hey, I can take you to the infirmary

586
00:40:22,280 --> 00:40:23,400
if you're not okay.

587
00:40:30,600 --> 00:40:32,240
- It's not serious.
- Good.

588
00:40:32,320 --> 00:40:33,880
Be careful during practice.

589
00:40:33,960 --> 00:40:34,960
Okay.

590
00:40:48,880 --> 00:40:50,600
Why are you following me?

591
00:40:50,680 --> 00:40:53,080
This class isn't over.
I have to stay with you.

592
00:40:54,920 --> 00:40:55,760
Hit me back.

593
00:40:55,840 --> 00:40:57,360
I won't dodge.

594
00:40:57,440 --> 00:40:58,720
Afterward, let's practice.

595
00:40:59,320 --> 00:41:02,280
This teacher is very strict
about substitutes.

596
00:41:02,360 --> 00:41:04,520
If I'm caught, I will be in big trouble.

597
00:41:06,360 --> 00:41:08,720
Afraid your Vitality Award will slip away?

598
00:41:09,520 --> 00:41:11,240
No, it's not that serious.

599
00:41:12,640 --> 00:41:13,600
What now, then?

600
00:41:42,960 --> 00:41:44,400
What are you waiting for?

601
00:41:44,480 --> 00:41:45,680
Get the ball.

602
00:42:02,200 --> 00:42:05,240
You two were recipients
of the Vitality Award in past years.

603
00:42:05,320 --> 00:42:07,600
First, thank you
for accepting this interview.

604
00:42:07,680 --> 00:42:10,080
Next, I will be asking you some questions.

605
00:42:10,160 --> 00:42:12,840
First, what does this award mean to you?

606
00:42:12,920 --> 00:42:14,000
- Money.
- Money.

607
00:42:16,040 --> 00:42:17,320
Do you need money too?

608
00:42:17,920 --> 00:42:19,120
No.

609
00:42:19,200 --> 00:42:21,120
Then why did you say money?

610
00:42:21,760 --> 00:42:23,320
Because it is money.

611
00:42:27,840 --> 00:42:30,520
How did you feel
when you received the award?

612
00:42:30,600 --> 00:42:31,480
- Relief.
- Relief.

613
00:42:38,520 --> 00:42:41,680
What would you want to do
if you had no worries?

614
00:42:41,760 --> 00:42:43,360
- Nothing at all.
- Nothing at all.

615
00:42:47,120 --> 00:42:48,080
Sorry,

616
00:42:48,160 --> 00:42:50,360
I'm going to ask an unrelated question.

617
00:42:50,440 --> 00:42:51,400
Are you acquainted?

618
00:42:52,080 --> 00:42:53,160
- No.
- No.

619
00:43:03,040 --> 00:43:04,560
<i>I said I didn't know him,</i>

620
00:43:04,640 --> 00:43:06,560
<i>and he said he didn't know me.</i>

621
00:43:06,640 --> 00:43:07,480
<i>It's true.</i>

622
00:43:08,480 --> 00:43:11,560
<i>We had met only a few times</i>
<i>at the hospital and in class.</i>

623
00:43:12,400 --> 00:43:14,440
<i>But sitting there that day,</i>

624
00:43:14,960 --> 00:43:17,120
<i>we seemed like we had</i>
<i>rehearsed our answers.</i>
